    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33750" root="فره" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرَاهٌ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُرَاتٌ</span>, as an epithet applied to water,
signifying <i>Sweet,</i> &amp;c.: both are chaste forms,
and well known, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَابُوهٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَابُوتٌ</span>: so in the
Towsheeh. (MF and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فرت</span>.)

